Perfect! I've completed the research. Here are my findings:

## 1. Simple Icons Plugin Location & Wiring

**Plugin Definition:** [plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/](plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/) — fully defined in [plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/src/index.ts).

**Is it wired in?** 
- ✅ **Yes, but opt-in at the component level** — not globally to the docs build
- `@pantoken/plugin-simple-icons` is listed as a devDependency in [docs/package.json](docs/package.json#L64)
- The docs site manually imports **specific** Simple Icons icons in Vue components via `@import` statements (e.g., [docs/.vitepress/theme/components/GetStartedTabs.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/GetStartedTabs.vue#L364-L373) imports `npm`, `pnpm`, `deno`, `bun`, `yarn`, `claudecode`, `googlegemini`, `cursor`, `githubcopilot`)
- There's no global `@import` of the simple-icons plugin CSS in the docs theme's main entry point

**How to reference an individual icon:**
- Package: `@pantoken/plugin-simple-icons`
- Export path: `./icons/<slug>.css` (e.g., `@pantoken/plugin-simple-icons/icons/html5.css`)
- Icon slug format: lowercase with hyphens (e.g., `"html5"`, `"github-actions"`)
- Export name (for token-layer code): Use `toExportName()` function from [src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/src/index.ts#L44) (converts `"github-actions"` → `"siGithubActions"`)

---

## 2. HTML5 Icon Availability & Naming

**✅ "html5" exists** — confirmed in the manifest at [plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/dist/manifest.json](plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/dist/manifest.json).

**Consuming code reference pattern:** The token name follows the `--instui-icon-<slug>` convention:
- **CSS custom property:** `--instui-icon-html5`
- **Glyph class:** `.-icon-html5` (used with the `icon` utility painter)
- **Modifier syntax:** Apply `.-icon-html5` to a glyph-painting element

Example from [plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/dist/icons/html5.css](plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/dist/icons/html5.css):
```css
:root { --instui-icon-html5: url('data:image/svg+xml;utf8,...'); }
.-icon-html5 { --pantoken-glyph: var(--instui-icon-html5); }
```

---

## 3. Icon Tokens Available at Docs Build Time

**What's globally available:**
- ✅ InstUI Lucide icons: `@pantoken/components/generated/icons.css` (imported in [index.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts#L21))
  - Contains `--instui-icon-*` tokens for ~500 Lucide icons (e.g., `--instui-icon-check`, `--instui-icon-alert`)
  - No Simple Icons in this sheet
- ✅ Custom icons: `@pantoken/plugin-custom-icons/generated/custom-icons.css` (imported in [index.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts#L23))
- ✅ Custom components: `@pantoken/plugin-custom-components/generated/custom-components.css` (imported in [index.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts#L22))

**What's NOT globally available:**
- ❌ Simple Icons are **NOT** auto-imported globally
- They must be selectively imported via `@import` in individual component `<style>` blocks

---

## 4. Build/Config Changes Required

**To add an html5 icon to `docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css` only:**

✅ **No build/config changes needed** — this is a **lightweight CSS-only change**

Simply add:
```css
@import "@pantoken/plugin-simple-icons/icons/html5.css";
```

Then reference it with:
```css
.platform.web::before {
  --pantoken-glyph: var(--instui-icon-html5);
}
```

**Why no config changes:**
- The simple-icons plugin is already wired as a devDependency in docs/package.json
- Individual icon CSS files are pre-built artifacts in `dist/icons/`
- No token pipeline re-configuration needed (Simple Icons live at the CSS asset level, not in the token IR)

---

## 5. CSS Custom Property Syntax for Icon Glyphs

**Pattern used elsewhere:** From [formats/components/src/utilities/icon-glyphs/index.ts](formats/components/src/utilities/icon-glyphs/index.ts#L27) and the generated output:

```css
/* Define the glyph token (already in --instui-icon-html5) */
:root {
  --instui-icon-html5: url('data:image/svg+xml;utf8,%3Csvg ...%3E');
}

/* Glyph class — apply this modifier to set the glyph variable */
.-icon-html5 {
  --pantoken-glyph: var(--instui-icon-html5);
}

/* Painter utility (shared ::before across all glyphs) — lives in @pantoken/components icon utilities */
.icon::before {
  content: '';
  display: inline-block;
  width: 1em;
  height: 1em;
  background-image: var(--pantoken-glyph);
  /* ... sizing/masking rules */
}
```

**For your `.platform.web` use case**, you would use:
```css
.platform.web::before {
  content: '';
  /* Apply glyph + painter sizing */
  --pantoken-glyph: var(--instui-icon-html5);
}
```

